@startuml receive-accelerator-channel-read
skinparam backgroundColor #F7FAFC
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #334155
  FontColor #0F172A
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}
skinparam activityDiamond {
  BorderColor #334155
  FontColor #0F172A
  BackgroundColor #E2E8F0
}
skinparam partition {
  BorderColor #334155
  FontColor #0F172A
}
skinparam note {
  BorderColor #334155
  FontColor #0F172A
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
}

start
:READ(h, c) under one read lock of the hot store state:
receive_occurrences(Some(h), c) reads a held handle h, and
current_receive_occurrences(c) reads h = receive_handle().
The lock fixes the live revision <latex>(\gamma_w, \sigma_w)</latex> = receive_revision()
and the live join view.; <<#E0E7FF>>
note right
  No handle: receive_occurrences(None, c), or a store
  without a published index, answers
  Fallback(vacant_receive_class()): Building while a
  build marker is open, Absent otherwise.
end note
partition "token_class(receive_revision()): the revision tokens of h" {
  if (shares_generation: <latex>\gamma_h = \gamma_w</latex> ?) then (no)
    :Fallback(Foreign); <<#FEE2E2>>
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  if (<latex>\sigma_h = \sigma_w</latex> ?) then (no)
    :Fallback(Stale); <<#FFEDD5>>
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
}
partition "join_scope_class(h.scope(), joins, c): the join groups of c" {
  if (J1: is the join prefix of c loaded in the live join view?\ntry_visit_join_groups returns Some) then (no)
    :Fallback(Incomplete); <<#EDE9FE>>
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  if (J2: is every join group g of c loaded in h.scope(),\nthe scope of the handle and never the live scope (D3)?\nis_loaded_prefix(continuation_prefix(g))) then (no)
    :Fallback(Incomplete); <<#EDE9FE>>
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
}
partition "h.materialize(c): the occurrence keys of c in the index of h" {
  :visit the keys under channel_frame(c) in the occurrence
  index of h with try_visit_groups_of, one group prefix per key;
  if (J3: is every visited group loaded in the snapshot of h?\nloaded_group_channels(prefix) is Some) then (no)
    :Fallback(Incomplete); <<#EDE9FE>>
    stop
  else (yes)
  endif
  :Exact(ReceiveOccurrences), stamped with revision() of h; <<#DCFCE7>>
  note right
    Each ReceiveOccurrenceGroup carries
    · the channels and prefix of its join group;
    · the positions of c, from the group prefix (positions_of);
    · its targets: the installed slot first (installed_entry),
      then the resting records in ordered_resting_records order.
    receive_id(target) = ReceiveId(revision, target), and
    resolve_receive answers only at an equal revision
    and for a byte-identical record.
  end note
}
stop

floating note left
  <b>Hydration issues no new revision.</b>
  hydrate_receive_scope(c) loads the join groups and the
  unloaded installed groups of c from history through
  get_continuations_versioned, which calls set_group:
  count_load increments loads and the published index
  is maintained, but <latex>\gamma</latex> and <latex>\sigma</latex> stay unchanged.
  A handle taken before the load keeps equal tokens, so
  J2 or J3 against its own scope answers Incomplete,
  and a handle taken after the load answers Exact.
end note

legend right
  |= Color |= Meaning |
  |<#E0E7FF> indigo | the read and its read lock |
  |<#E2E8F0> grey diamond | a check, asked in order; the first failure decides |
  |<#FEE2E2> red | Foreign: another generation |
  |<#FFEDD5> orange | Stale: the store token moved |
  |<#EDE9FE> violet | Incomplete: a join group outside the scope of h |
  |<#DCFCE7> green | Exact: the only answer from the accelerator |
  | Fallback(class) | the caller derives from the roots or fails closed |
endlegend
@enduml
